    {
      "request": "d09726f45f9ded6c921188736ae87996aaaeac52fece2f7cd2ab64e7ab50eda1",
      "response": {
        "content": "I couldn't confirm that the purchase order for REQ-1 went through, so I reported it as \"unknown\".\n\n- **Supplier choice:** I picked S-1 at 5.40 USD per unit, which is under the 6.00 cap. S-2 quoted 5.75. For 100 units that is 54,000 minor units (540.00 USD) charged to CC-OPS. Approval APR-0001 was granted for that amount.\n- **Rejected submission:** The submission came back as rejected with two failed checks. One said the approval had already been used, citing effect PO-0001. The other said the CC-OPS budget had changed since I read it.\n- **Evidence the order exists:** The CC-OPS committed amount went from 20,000 to 74,000, an increase of exactly 54,000. That suggests PO-0001 was actually placed despite the rejection message.\n- **Why I stopped:** I didn't resubmit, because that could create a duplicate order. The final report notes PO-0001 so someone can check whether it exists.\n\nThe final report system wouldn't accept an effect ID on an \"unknown\" claim, so PO-0001 appears only in the claim's note.",
